1
00:00:00,190 --> 00:00:04,110
Hephaestus, who would become the
greatest craftsman among the gods.

2
00:00:04,182 --> 00:00:07,538
But he was born lame, and
Hera was ashamed of him.

3
00:00:07,538 --> 00:00:09,322
She threw him off Olympus.

4
00:00:09,418 --> 00:00:11,847
Two sea goddesses caught him as he fell.

5
00:00:11,847 --> 00:00:15,156
For nine years he lived in
a cave beneath the waves,

6
00:00:15,156 --> 00:00:19,014
making jewellery for them, and
no other god knew he was alive.

7
00:00:19,014 --> 00:00:21,829
A later tradition says
he took his revenge.

8
00:00:21,970 --> 00:00:26,247
When he was grown, he sent his
mother a gift: a golden throne.

9
00:00:26,404 --> 00:00:30,141
Hera sat down, and invisible
chains closed around her.

10
00:00:30,141 --> 00:00:31,479
She could not stand.

11
00:00:31,479 --> 00:00:34,559
Hephaestus refused to come
to Olympus and free her.
